title: vcvt.f32.f64: just below 2^-126 is flushed, a NaN is the default NaN, -1e300 overflows to -inf
ref: A8.8 VCVT (between double-precision and single-precision) T1; A2.7 FPDoubleToSingle(), FPRound() (FPSCR = 0x03000000 on iOS (DN, FZ, round to nearest; ADR 0022)): exponent < -126 gives FPZero before rounding; overflow rounding to nearest gives infinity

[code]
b7eec08b    vcvt.f32.f64 s16, d0
f7eec28b    vcvt.f32.f64 s17, d2
b7eec39b    vcvt.f32.f64 s18, d3
7047        bx lr

[in]
d0 = 0x380FFFFFFFF80000     # 2^-126 - 2^-160: would round to 2^-126
d2 = 0x7FF0000000000123
d3 = f64:-1e300

[out]
s16 = 0
s17 = 0x7FC00000
s18 = 0xFF800000
